.TH MW-RUN 1 "2026-07-03" "MemoryWhale" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw-run \- run a command and capture its output into MemoryWhale
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw-run
.RI [ --cwd
.IR path ]
.RI [ --notes
.IR text ]
.B --
.I command
.RI [ args... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw-run
runs
.I command
to completion, streaming its output to your terminal as usual, while saving a
copy \(em command, arguments, working directory, exit code, stdout, and stderr
\(em into the local MemoryWhale SQLite database. Captured output is scrubbed for
common secrets before storage (see
.BR mw (1)).
.B mw-run
exits with the same status as the command it ran. Nothing is uploaded.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--cwd " path
Directory to run the command in (default: the current directory).
.TP
.BI "--notes " text
Free-form note attached to the run.
.TP
.B --
Everything after this is the command and its arguments.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
mw-run --notes "check the backend" -- cargo check
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw (1),
.BR mw-remember (1),
.BR mw-serve (1)
